# EE 471 – Week 6: Docker & Cog

## Requirements
- Docker Desktop
- Cog (`brew install replicate/tap/cog`)
- An Azure Speech resource (for Task 1)

## Task 1 – Containerized speech studio & voice calculator

Create `task1/.env`:
```
SPEECH_KEY=your-key
SPEECH_REGION=westeurope
```

Speech studio:
```bash
cd task1/speech-studio
docker build -t speech-studio .
docker run --rm --name speech-studio -p 5001:5001 --env-file ../.env speech-studio
```
Open http://localhost:5001

Voice calculator:
```bash
cd task1/voice-calculator
docker build -t voice-calculator .
docker run --rm --name voice-calculator -p 5002:5001 --env-file ../.env voice-calculator
```
Open http://localhost:5002

## Task 2 – Cat-kind classifier (Cog + Flask)

Build the model image with Cog, then start the model and the website:
```bash
cd task2/cat-model
cog build -t cat-model
cd ..
docker compose up --build
```
Open http://localhost:8000, upload a cat image and click **Classify**.

Live prediction logs from inside the model container:
```bash
docker exec -it cat-model tail -f /tmp/predictions.log
```

Direct API call to the Cog container (JSON only; images as base64 data URI):
```bash
curl http://localhost:5050/predictions -X POST \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d "{\"input\": {\"image\": \"data:image/jpeg;base64,$(base64 -i cat.jpg)\"}}"
```

## Docker intro
`getting-started-todo-app/` is the sample project from Docker's "Introduction" tutorial.